-- =========================================================================
-- module pages where — POST /p/:accountSlug/:pageSlug/submit orchestration.
--
-- module-substrate Phase 3n (2026-05-31) — the AGGREGATION-DISSOLVE
-- representative. The retired `engine/src/modules/public-surfaces.ts` was a
-- junk-drawer BUNDLE: it loaded THIS file (under the throwaway internal name
-- `pages-ingress`) AND `receipt/ingress.fenel` (`receipt-ingress`), hand-
-- extracted each body by id, re-wrapped every function in a `defineFunction`
-- spec, re-prefixed to the public `pages:` / `receipt:` namespaces, and
-- exported ONE `publicSurfacesModule` holding all 6. Nothing consumed the
-- bundle as a semantic unit (it was imported by name only in the 4 boot
-- lists), so per the standing steer ("no wrapper modules around already-clean
-- separate modules — make semantic modules") it is DISSOLVED: `pages` and
-- `receipt` become their own modules and the lump is deleted.
--
-- THIS file is now a `module pages where` source-of-truth: header + the 4
-- `pages:*` sigs + their @label/@description/@tags identity facets (lifted
-- from the retired `defineFunction` specs). Bodies are unchanged. No stored
-- @category — the `pages` category derives at read time from the `pages:` id
-- prefix (Phase 3j). None of the 4 carried an `@ioAction` (IOInvokable ×0).
-- The `HasStateIO` requires on submitPage + dispatchPageSubmittedIfFlow are
-- INFERRED transitively from their `state:*` / event calls
-- (attachInferredRequires), not hand-declared (the 3a precedent).
--
-- Phase 12c-routes sub-step 3 of the ts-elimination workstream (origin). The
-- TS route is now a THIN HTTP leaf — routing + c.req.param/header/json + the
-- state:getPageBySlug invoke + formBlock find (wire-shape discrimination) +
-- HTTP status mapping. Everything ELSE is Fenel (storage-as-effect Phase 4f):
--   - GET assembly → pages:pageView (resolveType the typeRef + serve the raw
--     $record `type` so the widget renders via FieldRenderer — mirror of
--     types:formView; the page widget extracts fields via fieldsOf(form.type))
--   - typeRef resolution + validation → folded into submitPage via the shared
--     types:resolveType + account-aware state:validateEntityInstance boundary
--   - the visitor ip + the page config Maybes → BUILT in the body from the raw
--     header/JSON values (truthy-gated), not pre-marshalled TS-side
--
-- submitPage composes (storage-as-effect Phase 4f):
--   1. types:resolveType typeRef → Nothing → { error = "Type not found: …" }
--      (the system-entity arm covers the live `profile` page); Just row →
--      thread the CANONICAL type name (row.name).
--   2. state:validateEntityInstance row.name data false — the account's
--      UUID-identified field registry supplies types/facets and returns the
--      canonical coerced value. not ok → { error }.
--   3. state:tryCreateInstanceByName row.name validation.value (storage-as-effect Phase 4a —
--      the submitted data is an INSTANCE of the resolved type, mirroring
--      types:submit; NO dedicated page_submissions row). ok false → { error }.
--   4. appendEvent "submitted" — UNCONDITIONAL, anchored to the PAGE aggregate
--      (aggregateType = Just "page", aggregateId = Just pageId). The visitor `ip`
--      (built into a Maybe<String> from the raw header value) rides the PAYLOAD
--      (durable submission metadata; the event is its source of truth). The
--      dispatchEventTriggers fan-out stays flow-gated on formBlock.flowId.
--   5. response: { redirect = url } when config.redirectUrl is present, else
--      { message = thankYouMessage } with the default magic string verbatim (Risk 5).
--
-- storage-as-effect Phase 4a (2026-06-19) — the page-submit lane collapse (D4
-- slice 1). createPageSubmission + the page_submissions table RETIRED; capture
-- is the generic state:tryCreateInstanceByName, exactly like types:submit.
--
-- Decisions resolved / RETIRED:
--   Z   RETIRED (storage-as-effect Phase 4f) — resolveFormFields is GONE; the
--       page GET serves the raw `type` (pages:pageView), not a TS-extracted
--       fields array. Fenel-first overrides Decision Z's "stays TS".
--   AA  RETIRED (storage-as-effect Phase 4f / field-identity Phase 2b) —
--       validation is the account-aware state:validateEntityInstance boundary.
--       The TS @fenel/core validate() + the recordType rebuild + the
--       listFunctions/overlayUserFunctions/getSystemEvaluateContext machinery
--       are DELETED. (D-VALIDATE: one identified registry + coercion boundary.)
--   BB  (no JSONB-key navigation needed here — config fields are static-keyed)
--   EE  (pages /submit is profileId-less per pre-12c-3 — no auth context)
--
-- parseApp doesn't continue conditionals/arg-lists across newlines ⇒ the
-- resolve→validate→create→emit pipeline factors into top-level helpers
-- (the submit.fenel recipe). resolveType is the shared types:* resolver;
-- truthy/ifElse/find/eq/head are std.
-- =========================================================================

module pages where

-- pageView — what GET /p/:accountSlug/:pageSlug serves: the page chrome
-- (slug / name / config) + the resolved type's RAW $record `type` (so the
-- public page widget renders the fields via fieldsOf(form.type) → FieldRenderer,
-- exactly like the forms widget). storage-as-effect Phase 4f: PORTS the route's
-- former resolveFormFields + the {page, form} assembly into Fenel (Decision Z
-- RETIRED). The TS route resolves the page (state:getPageBySlug — a leaf) +
-- finds the formBlock (wire-shape), then invokes this with accountId =
-- page.accountId so resolveType is account-scoped. Nothing (type unresolvable)
-- → the route maps to 404.
@label "Page view"
@description "storage-as-effect Phase 4f / field-identity Phase 2b — GET /p/:accountSlug/:pageSlug's response. types:resolveType typeRef → Nothing (404) | Just row → { page, form = { typeName = row.name, type = row.type, submitLabel, typeRef } }. typeName lets the browser select the registry-local identified definition before planning; raw row.type remains the public wire definition."
@tags "page" "view" "route" "storage-as-effect"
pageView : String -> String -> String -> String -> Map String Any -> Maybe ({ page: { slug: String, name: String, config: Map String Any }, form: { typeName: String, type: Type, submitLabel: String, typeRef: String, rootBinding: { origin: String, id: String, name: String } } })
pageView slug name typeRef submitLabel config =
  case resolveType typeRef of
    Nothing -> Nothing
    Just row -> Just (pageViewOf slug name typeRef submitLabel config row)

-- pageViewOf — assemble the served { page, form } record from the resolved
-- type row. Pure record transform (the page/form objects are let-bound so
-- parseApp doesn't fight a multi-line record literal).
@label "Page view (assemble)"
@description "storage-as-effect Phase 4f — assemble GET /p/:accountSlug/:pageSlug's { page = { slug, name, config }, form = { type = row.type, submitLabel, typeRef } } from the resolved type row. Pure record transform."
@tags "page" "view" "pure" "storage-as-effect"
pageViewOf : String -> String -> String -> String -> Map String Any -> ({ id: String, name: String, type: Type }) -> { page: { slug: String, name: String, config: Map String Any }, form: { typeName: String, type: Type, submitLabel: String, typeRef: String, rootBinding: { origin: String, id: String, name: String } } }
pageViewOf slug name typeRef submitLabel config row =
  let pageObj = { slug = slug, name = name, config = config }
  let formObj = { typeName = row.name, type = row.type, submitLabel = submitLabel, typeRef = typeRef, rootBinding = publicTypeRootBinding row }
  { page = pageObj, form = formObj }

-- submitPage — the POST /p/:accountSlug/:pageSlug/submit orchestration body.
-- storage-as-effect Phase 4f: the typeRef resolution + validation are FOLDED
-- IN (Decisions Z/AA retired) — the SAME resolve → validate → capture → emit
-- loop the forms lane runs (types:submitValidate), with the page-anchored emit +
-- redirect/message response as the page lane's distinct tail. Per parseApp's
-- multi-line rule, each branch factors into a top-level helper.
--
-- Inputs:
--   pageId         — String (page entity id; the appendEvent aggregate)
--   pageSlug       — String (the submitted event payload)
--   typeRef        — String (formBlock.typeRef; resolved IN Fenel now)
--   data           — Record (raw submission data; validated in-body)
--   ip             — String (raw visitor ip header value, "" when absent;
--                    the body builds the Maybe<String> for the event payload)
--   flowConfigured — Boolean (true when formBlock.flowId is set; gates the
--                    dispatchEventTriggers fan-out per pre-12c-3 semantics)
--   config         — Record (raw page.config; drives the redirect vs message
--                    response — the body reads its fields directly, no Maybe
--                    pre-marshalling)
@label "Submit page"
@description "Phase 2b UUID-only field convergence — POST /p/:accountSlug/:pageSlug/submit resolves the public typeRef, validates once through state:validateEntityInstance with the account's identified field registry, persists the coerced validation.value, and emits the page-anchored submitted event."
@tags "page" "ingress" "route" "storage-as-effect" "field-identity"
submitPage : String -> String -> String -> {} -> String -> Boolean -> {} -> {}
submitPage pageId pageSlug typeRef data ip flowConfigured config =
  case resolveType typeRef of
    Nothing -> { error = `Type not found: ${typeRef}` }
    Just row -> submitPageCapture pageId pageSlug row.name data ip flowConfigured config

-- submitPageCapture — the account-aware validation gate. Only the coerced
-- validation.value can reach persistence and event/flow payloads.
@label "Submit page (validate)"
@description "Phase 2b UUID-only field convergence — validate raw public input through state:validateEntityInstance using the canonical type name and account field registry; persist and emit only validation.value."
@tags "page" "ingress" "validate" "storage-as-effect" "field-identity"
submitPageCapture : String -> String -> String -> {} -> String -> Boolean -> {} -> {}
submitPageCapture pageId pageSlug typeName data ip flowConfigured config =
  let validation = validateEntityInstance typeName data false
  if validation.ok
  then submitPageCreate pageId pageSlug typeName validation.value ip flowConfigured config
  else { error = pageValidationMessage validation.errors }

-- pageValidationMessage — retain the route's string error envelope while the
-- account-aware validation substrate remains structured.
pageValidationMessage : List a -> String
@label "Page validation message"
@description "Project the first structured state:validateEntityInstance error into the public page error string envelope."
@tags "page" "ingress" "validate" "field-identity"
pageValidationMessage errors =
  case head errors of
    Nothing -> "Validation failed"
    Just error -> error.message

-- submitPageCreate — the unverified capture. state:tryCreateInstanceByName of
-- the CANONICAL type name (mirroring types:submitCreate); ok → emit, not ok →
-- { error } carrying the insert error.
@label "Submit page (create)"
@description "storage-as-effect Phase 4f — the capture arm of submitPage. state:tryCreateInstanceByName typeName data persists an INSTANCE of the resolved type (mirroring types:submit — no dedicated page_submissions row). ok → submitPageEmit, not ok → { error = the insert error }."
@tags "page" "ingress" "create" "storage-as-effect"
submitPageCreate : String -> String -> String -> {} -> String -> Boolean -> {} -> {}
submitPageCreate pageId pageSlug typeName data ip flowConfigured config =
  let r = tryCreateInstanceByName typeName data
  if r.ok
  then submitPageEmit pageId pageSlug typeName data ip flowConfigured config r.value
  else { error = r.error }

-- submitPageEmit — the successful-capture tail. Builds the visitor ip Maybe
-- from the raw header value (truthy-gated — absent/"" → Nothing), fires the
-- `submitted` event (unconditional appendEvent, ip in the payload) anchored to
-- the page aggregate, runs the flow-gated dispatchEventTriggers fan-out, and
-- returns the redirect-vs-message response.
@label "Submit page (emit)"
@description "storage-as-effect Phase 4a / Phase 4c / Phase 4f — successful-capture tail of submitPage. Builds the visitor ip Maybe<String> from the raw header value (truthy-gated, replacing the retired TS pre-marshalling), then writes the `submitted` event (renamed from page_submitted in Phase 4c — no form/funnel noun; one event unifies the form/page lanes; payload { type = the canonical type name, instanceId, pageSlug, data, ip }; aggregateType = Just \"page\", aggregateId = Just pageId), runs the flow-gated dispatchEventTriggers fan-out, and returns the redirect-vs-message response shape."
@tags "page" "ingress" "emit" "storage-as-effect"
submitPageEmit : String -> String -> String -> {} -> String -> Boolean -> {} -> String -> {}
submitPageEmit pageId pageSlug typeName data ip flowConfigured config instanceId =
  let ipM = ifElse (truthy ip) (Just ip) Nothing
  let _appended = appendEvent "submitted" { type = typeName, instanceId = instanceId, pageSlug = pageSlug, data = data, ip = ipM } (Just "page") (Just pageId) Nothing
  let _dispatched = dispatchPageSubmittedIfFlow flowConfigured pageSlug pageId typeName data
  pageResponse config

-- dispatchPageSubmittedIfFlow — fires the dispatchEventTriggers fan-out
-- only when formBlock.flowId is configured (pre-12c-3 semantics: the
-- appendEvent is unconditional, the trigger fan-out is gated).
@label "Dispatch page-submitted if flow"
@description "Phase 12c-routes sub-step 3 / Phase 4c — gates the dispatchEventTriggers fan-out on formBlock.flowId presence (pre-12c-3 semantics: appendEvent unconditional, trigger fan-out gated). Fires the `submitted` trigger event (renamed from page_submitted in Phase 4c)."
@tags "page" "pure" "phase-12c"
dispatchPageSubmittedIfFlow : Boolean -> String -> String -> String -> {} -> {}
dispatchPageSubmittedIfFlow flowConfigured pageSlug pageId typeName data =
  let payload = { page = data, pageSlug = pageSlug, pageId = pageId, type = typeName }
  let dispatchArm = dispatchEventTriggers "submitted" payload
  let skipArm = {}
  ifElse flowConfigured dispatchArm skipArm

-- pageResponse — decide redirect-vs-message based on config.redirectUrl.
-- storage-as-effect Phase 4f: reads the RAW page.config (no Maybe pre-marshalling
-- — the TS configForBody is retired). truthy config.redirectUrl (present + non-
-- empty) → redirect, else the thank-you message.
@label "Page response"
@description "Phase 12c-routes sub-step 3 / storage-as-effect Phase 4f — decide redirect-vs-message from the RAW page.config (the TS configForBody Maybe-marshalling is retired). truthy config.redirectUrl → { redirect = config.redirectUrl }, else { message = pageThankYouMessage config }. Pure record transform."
@tags "page" "pure" "phase-12c"
pageResponse : {} -> {}
pageResponse config =
  ifElse (truthy config.redirectUrl)
    { redirect = config.redirectUrl }
    { message = pageThankYouMessage config }

-- pageThankYouMessage — default to the magic-string "Thank you for your
-- submission!" when config.thankYouMessage is absent. Risk 5 — preserve
-- the default verbatim for wire-shape equivalence. Reads the raw config
-- field directly (storage-as-effect Phase 4f).
@label "Page thank-you message"
@description "Phase 12c-routes sub-step 3 / storage-as-effect Phase 4f — default to the magic-string 'Thank you for your submission!' when the raw config.thankYouMessage is absent/empty (truthy-gated). Preserves the pre-12c-3 default verbatim (Risk 5)."
@tags "page" "pure" "phase-12c"
pageThankYouMessage : {} -> String
pageThankYouMessage config =
  ifElse (truthy config.thankYouMessage) config.thankYouMessage "Thank you for your submission!"
